{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 7 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        \n        long[] a = new long[17];\n        a[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i < 17; i++) {\n            a[i] = a[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        long result = solve(n, a);\n        pw.println(result);\n        pw.close();\n        br.close();\n    }\n    \n    private static long solve(int n, long[] a) {\n        Map<Long, Long> cache = new HashMap<>();\n        return calc(n, a, cache);\n    }\n    \n    private static long calc(long n, long[] a, Map<Long, Long> cache) {\n        if (n == 0) return 0;\n        Long cached = cache.get(n);\n        if (cached != null) return cached;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < 17; i++) {\n            if (a[i] >= n) {\n                if (a[i] == n) {\n                    long result = i + 1;\n                    cache.put(n, result);\n                    return result;\n                }\n                \n                long k = n / a[i - 1];\n                long c1 = i * k + calc(n - a[i - 1] * k, a, cache);\n                \n                long diff = a[i] - n;\n                k = diff / a[i - 1];\n                long c2 = i + 1 + i * k + calc(a[i] - a[i - 1] * k - n, a, cache);\n                \n                long min = Math.min(c1, c2);\n                cache.put(n, min);\n                return min;\n            }\n        }\n        throw new RuntimeException(\"Failed for n=\" + n);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        \n        long[] a = new long[17];\n        a[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i < 17; i++) {\n            a[i] = a[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        long result = solve(n, a);\n        pw.println(result);\n        pw.close();\n        br.close();\n    }\n    \n    private static long solve(int n, long[] a) {\n        Map<Long, Long> cache = new HashMap<>();\n        return calc(n, a, cache);\n    }\n    \n    private static long calc(long n, long[] a, Map<Long, Long> cache) {\n        if (n == 0) return 0;\n        if (n < 0) return Integer.MAX_VALUE; // Invalid case\n        Long cached = cache.get(n);\n        if (cached != null) return cached;\n        \n        long min = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < 17; i++) {\n            if (a[i] > n) {\n                // Try using a[i-1] with positive and negative coefficients\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    // Only 1 available\n                    long result = n;\n                    cache.put(n, result);\n                    return result;\n                }\n                \n                // Option 1: use a[i-1] multiple times\n                long k = n / a[i-1];\n                long remainder = n % a[i-1];\n                long c1 = i * k + calc(remainder, a, cache);\n                \n                // Option 2: use a[i] and subtract some a[i-1] terms\n                long diff = a[i] - n;\n                if (diff <= n) { // Only consider if it's not too expensive\n                    long k2 = diff / a[i-1];\n                    if (k2 > 0) {\n                        long c2 = (i + 1) + i * k2 + calc(a[i] - a[i-1] * k2 - n, a, cache);\n                        min = Math.min(min, Math.min(c1, c2));\n                    } else {\n                        min = Math.min(min, c1);\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    min = Math.min(min, c1);\n                }\n                \n                cache.put(n, min);\n                return min;\n            } else if (a[i] == n) {\n                long result = i + 1;\n                cache.put(n, result);\n                return result;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Fallback: use all 1s\n        long result = n;\n        cache.put(n, result);\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00010644822759786621, -2.7418097943154862e-06, 0.0, -9.298280929215252e-06, -1.4543427823809907e-0